{"authored" [{"question" "q-114138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1,$ then what is ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+1 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3(3-(-1)) \\\\  & =6-3(4) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5d0ec2c5848b8f24d1396021f59046d97eba12d3520c179fc90f3c2667188de" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d76912d15295676bb4fc66684a8bac36118bdf2205aeb877ef35e8ddf3f69d" "basis" 1293 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037749/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{6}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-4798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{6}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3+5 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-4798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec074b36716a9ea8e20e6a66e2b639608de20588b4549d3a1bb063ca4f95a325"} {"question" "q-4798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-4798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-4798" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-73340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4$, calculate\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}(7f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-73340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{3}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(7f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & =7{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7(4)+2\\cdot x\\,{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =28+2(3-1) \\\\  & =28+4 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-73340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec074b36716a9ea8e20e6a66e2b639608de20588b4549d3a1bb063ca4f95a325"} {"question" "q-73340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-73340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "23"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-73340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(x)-6x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(x)-6x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-3({1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =1-3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec074b36716a9ea8e20e6a66e2b639608de20588b4549d3a1bb063ca4f95a325"} {"question" "q-114019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1,$ then what is ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+1 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3(3-(-1)) \\\\  & =6-3(4) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec074b36716a9ea8e20e6a66e2b639608de20588b4549d3a1bb063ca4f95a325"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-114138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ (-5){\\int }_{7}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ 5{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec074b36716a9ea8e20e6a66e2b639608de20588b4549d3a1bb063ca4f95a325"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "685b6f77acc47b81121acfc73d90178ffe451acbd5538ee405208d7d1a504f48"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/De